    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "adb23a44_a77d4101",
        "filename": "gm/BazelGMRunner.cpp",
        "patchSetId": 8
      },
      "lineNbr": 290,
      "author": {
        "id": 5395
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-07-19T13:29:02Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I originally thought \"Could we make our known vias a class enum and then turn this into a switch statement?\"\n\nHowever, one reason we might *not* want to use an enum and an if statement is because having all the vias in this way couples them together.\n\nAs things are currently written, we *must* have SkPicture support to compile BazelGMRunner.cpp now. If something changes the SkPicture implementation, we would have to re-compile and re-run all tests, not just those which use the serialization via, because the linker cannot throw away the serialization/deserialization code.\n\nI think we might want each via to be defined in its own file and implement the same interface (draw). That way, at build time, we can only bring in what we need.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 290,
        "startChar": 35,
        "endLine": 290,
        "endChar": 48
      },
      "revId": "01d0cc99361bcb0bb6ce877c4f360e5ead1ed051",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "c12fd5b8_fc22f106",
        "filename": "gm/BazelGMRunner.cpp",
        "patchSetId": 8
      },
      "lineNbr": 290,
      "author": {
        "id": 5395
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-07-19T13:41:11Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "After looking at the follow-on CL, here\u0027s what I think will work cleanly and also reduce unnecessary duplication.\n\nForward declare (or make a header for) the function\n```\nGMOutput draw(skiagm::GM* gm, SkSurface* surface, std::string via)\n```\n(or `draw_with_via(...)`, if you prefer)\n\nAdd a new file DirectVia.cpp which will have the current implementation of draw()\n\nAdd a new file PictureVias.cpp which declares draw() and looks at the via param to decide if it should deserialize the picture and then draw it or just draw the picture directly.\n\nThe build rules will then bundle in the appropriate via .cpp file, effectively making a new binary for a surface+via combination.",
      "parentUuid": "adb23a44_a77d4101",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 290,
        "startChar": 35,
        "endLine": 290,
        "endChar": 48
      },
      "revId": "01d0cc99361bcb0bb6ce877c4f360e5ead1ed051",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
